      notes: - Plan steps 1-2 said to swap to `use ark_ec::PrimeGroup;` and asserted "no per-site rewrites needed" because only `EdwardsProjective::generator()` was thought to need a trait. In practice, the bench files also call `.double()` on `EdwardsProjective`, which in ark-ec 0.5 lives on the `AdditiveGroup` supertrait (in `ark_ff`, re-exported as `ark_ec::AdditiveGroup`) and must be in scope independently. Without it, `cargo check --benches` failed with `E0599: no method named 'double'`. To satisfy the plan's verify gate (`! grep -E "^error"`) with the smallest, most conservative change, I imported both: `use ark_ec::{AdditiveGroup, PrimeGroup};`. This mirrors the existing pattern at `src/crypto/jubjub.rs:11` (`use ark_ec::AdditiveGroup;`) and still removes the `Group as ArkGroup` alias as required. The `! grep -q "ark_ec::Group as ArkGroup"` verify check still passes.
